Question 3
What are the financial concerns highlighted in the passage caused by the rise in referral cases? Mention the initiatives that the government has taken to lower lifestyle-related diseases among Bhutanese citizens. (10 marks)', 'Financial concerns: referral costs are rising sharply. The health ministry spent about Nu 206.7 million in 2021-22, Nu 501 million in 2022-23 and Nu 529.95 million from 2023 to April 2024 - an increase of 154.3% between 2021 and 2023 and about Nu 1.2 billion in total, with another Nu 80-100 million needed until June 2024. A single referral, like Nima''s, cost over Nu 300,000 - nearly twice his annual salary - plus allowances for the patient and escort. Over 1,000 patients were referred in less than a year and numbers keep rising, while some doctors feel the prevention budget is too small to make an impact.
Government initiatives: the Department of Public Health runs awareness and advocacy programmes, sharing infographics through social media and information on salt intake, early detection, screening and how NCDs can be prevented; the health system follows the primary health care model that emphasises prevention; the capital budget for prevention rose from Nu 1 billion in the 12th Plan to about Nu 5 billion proposed in the 13th FYP (from 15% to 30% of the budget); and the first Cath Lab at JDWNRH (September 2023) has reduced heart referrals from 15-20 to three or four a month, with an open-heart surgery team planned by mid-2025.', null, '[{"point": "Financial concerns with figures: Nu 206.7 m (2021-22) to Nu 501 m (2022-23) and Nu 529.95 m (2023-April 2024), 154.3% rise 2021-2023, Nu 1.2 billion total, extra Nu 80-100 m needed; one referral (Nu 300,000) nearly twice a driver''s annual salary; prevention budget said to be too small", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Initiatives: awareness and advocacy by DoPH (social media infographics, salt intake, early detection, screening), primary health care model, prevention budget Nu 1 billion (12th Plan) to Nu 5 billion (13th FYP), share raised 15% to 30%, Cath Lab at JDWNRH and planned open-heart team", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'english-general-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'english-general-knowledge') and t.slug = 'case-study-and-comprehension'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-2'), 'standard', 10,
