  values ('ME', 'long_answer', '"Pemagatshel''s mango growers face marketing challenges amid rising production" - BBS, August 2024
"Garja Man Rai, a 79-year-old farmer in Woongchilo Chiwog of Tareythang Gewog, Sarpang, has begun harvesting mangoes and bananas from the million-fruit-tree plantation" - Kuensel, 9 July 2024
These two statements show that Bhutan is moving towards self-sufficiency in nutritious fruit and food production through the government''s million fruit tree plantation project. However, the excess production of fruit may be wasted.
Elaborate two means the government can provide to help farmers get easy access to local and international markets. Discuss three ways citizens can play their role to grab this opportunity and become economically independent. (10 marks)', 'The million fruit tree plantation has started to bear fruit, but without markets the surplus will rot.
Two means the government can provide:
1. Market infrastructure and linkages: build collection centres, cold storage and pack houses in producing gewogs, improve farm roads and transport, and link farmers directly to buyers - schools and institutions, hotels, the Food Corporation of Bhutan''s buy-back schemes and online marketplaces - so produce reaches local markets quickly.
2. Export support: help farmers meet quality, phytosanitary and organic certification standards, negotiate access through trade agreements (e.g. with India and Bangladesh), brand Bhutanese fruit (such as Pemagatshel mangoes) and share market information.
Three ways citizens can take this opportunity:
1. Value addition: start small processing enterprises - mango juice, pickles, jam, dried fruit and chips - which last longer and sell at higher prices.
2. Organise: form cooperatives or farmer groups to sell in bulk, share transport and cold storage, and bargain for better prices.
3. Use digital marketing: sell through social media, e-commerce platforms and direct contracts with shops and hotels, and explore agri-tourism such as fruit-picking visits.
In this way surplus fruit becomes income, and young people and farmers can become economically independent.', null, '[{"point": "Two government means: market infrastructure and linkages (cold storage, collection centres, transport, buy-back by FCBL, school feeding/ institutional buyers, online platforms), export support (certification, quality standards, trade agreements, branding, export market information) ", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Three citizen roles: value addition/ processing (juice, pickles, dried fruit, jam), forming cooperatives/ farmer groups for bulk selling, using e-commerce and social media marketing, agri-tourism, quality and organic production, entrepreneurship and loans", "marks": 6}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'english-general-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'english-general-knowledge') and t.slug = 'topical-issues-economy-and-agriculture'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-2'), 'standard', 10,
    1080, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
