  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'With the drastic increase in the use of digital platforms, especially social media apps, hundreds of thousands of products and services are posted online, primarily on platforms like Facebook, Instagram, TikTok and Telegram.
Express your view on the importance of e-commerce. Highlight the advantages it provides to both the seller and the buyer, and point out the drawbacks it brings to the buyer and to the regulatory bodies. (10 marks)', 'E-commerce has become important in Bhutan: it lets anyone with a phone sell or buy goods and services, supports young entrepreneurs and small businesses, reaches rural customers and grows the digital economy along with mobile banking.
Advantages for sellers: very low start-up and running costs (no shop rent), access to customers across the country and abroad 24 hours a day, cheap marketing through posts and videos, direct communication with customers, and the chance to test products before expanding.
Advantages for buyers: convenience of shopping from home, wide choice, easy price comparison, home delivery and reviews from other customers.
Drawbacks for buyers: fraud and fake or poor-quality products that differ from the pictures; no clear return or refund policy; delays or loss in delivery; and risks to personal data and online payments.
Drawbacks for regulatory bodies: many online sellers are unregistered and unlicensed, so it is difficult to collect taxes, enforce consumer protection and quality standards, trace fraudsters, or stop the sale of illegal, unsafe or counterfeit goods, especially from sellers outside the country; it also raises cyber-crime and data protection problems.
Therefore e-commerce should be encouraged, with simple online business registration, consumer protection rules, secure payment systems and public awareness.', null, '[{"point": "View on importance: growing economy, convenience, jobs for youth, small businesses, rural access, digital payments", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Advantages to sellers: low start-up cost, wider market/ 24-7, direct contact, low overhead, marketing reach", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Advantages to buyers: convenience, choice, price comparison, home delivery, reviews", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Drawbacks to buyers: fraud/ fake products, no quality guarantee, delivery problems, no refund, privacy and payment risks", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Drawbacks to regulators: unregistered businesses, tax evasion, hard to monitor/ enforce consumer protection, illegal/ unsafe goods, cross-border sellers, data/ cyber crime", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'english-general-knowledge'),
