  values ('ME', 'descriptive', 'More than 25 countries have banned TikTok either fully or partially. Many South Asian nations banned this media app in 2020.
Discuss the benefits and effects it brings to the social well-being of citizens. Elaborate with reasons how it affects the security, privacy, harmony and sovereignty of the country. (10 marks)', 'TikTok, like other short-video apps, brings benefits to citizens: entertainment and relaxation; a platform for creativity, talent and self-expression; quick learning and awareness on health, farming, cooking and current issues; free marketing and income for small businesses and influencers; and promotion of Bhutanese culture and tourism. But it also has harmful effects on social well-being: addiction and loss of study and work time, especially among children and youth; effects on mental health and self-esteem; cyberbullying and exposure to inappropriate content; and the spread of rumours and misinformation.
Security: the app collects large amounts of user data, and some governments fear that a foreign company could be required to share it with its government; it can also be used for scams and cyber crime. Privacy: users'' locations, contacts, viewing habits and images may be stored and used without their full understanding. Harmony: viral false or divisive content, mocking of culture, religion or institutions, and online quarrels can harm social harmony and respect, which are central to Bhutanese values. Sovereignty: when a foreign platform''s algorithms decide what citizens see, a country has less control over its information space and is exposed to foreign influence.
Therefore, rather than relying only on bans, countries like Bhutan should strengthen data protection laws, regulate harmful content, promote digital and media literacy and encourage responsible use.', null, '[{"point": "Benefits: entertainment, creativity, learning/ awareness, marketing and income for small businesses, connecting people, promoting culture and tourism", "marks": 3}, {"point": "Negative social effects: addiction and time-wasting, mental health/ body image, cyberbullying, inappropriate content, misinformation, harm to children''s studies", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Security and privacy: data collection by foreign company, possible foreign access, surveillance, scams/ cyber crime", "marks": 2.5}, {"point": "Harmony and sovereignty: misinformation and divisive content, disrespect of culture/ institutions, foreign influence, weakening control over national information space; balance through regulation and digital literacy", "marks": 2.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'english-general-knowledge'),
